course: dictionary
lesson: 8074
title: Feelings that ease a worry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Relieved is a feeling word. It means happy and calm because something bad did not happen, or because a worry is over. Look at the clues around it. «Mia was scared, then relieved, and it was not her fault at all.» Scared comes first, then relieved, so relieved is the feeling that comes after the fear has gone.
explain: Look for what came before the feeling. «She's embarrassed, and also weirdly relieved she's not the only one.» The words not the only one tell you the worry was about being alone in something awkward. Relieved means that worry went away.
explain: Relieved can also be the past form of relieve. To relieve something is to make it less, or to take over a job so someone can rest. «The medicine relieved the pain» means the pain got smaller. A word can have more than one meaning, so check the clues each time.
fact: Relieved means feeling happy and calm because a worry is over.
fact: Relieved is the past form of relieve, which means to make pain or a problem less.
fact: Useful phrases: relieved to hear, relieved that, feel relieved, and breathe a sigh of relief.
fact: «People sometimes cry when they are very happy, proud or relieved.» So relieved can be a strong feeling, not only a quiet one.
fact: Health example: «The medicine relieved the pain» means the medicine made the pain less.
exercise: «Mia was scared, then relieved.» How does Mia feel at the end? | Angry and loud | *Happy and calm, because the worry is over | Bored and tired | Hungry and cold
exercise: «The medicine relieved the pain.» What does relieved mean here? | *Made the pain less | Gave the pain a name | Made the pain stronger | Made the pain go to sleep
exercise: Dad says, «I'm relieved to hear you're safe.» What does relieved to hear show? | Dad is hungry for dinner | Dad has lost his keys | Dad is angry and shouting | *Dad's worry is over, so he feels calm and glad
test: Nan says, «Let me relieve you at the wheel so you can rest.» What does relieve mean? | *To take over the job so you can rest | To make a mess of the car | To feel calm | To shout at the driver
test: «She's embarrassed, and also weirdly relieved she's not the only one.» Why is she relieved? | *Because she is not alone in feeling embarrassed | Because her bag is heavy | Because it is raining | Because she won a prize
exam: What does «relieved» most closely mean in «I felt relieved when the test was over»? | *Glad, because the worry was over | Angry about the test | Sad that it was short | Tired after running
